[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Accepted: Normal Variation, Traditional System"]
[ECO "D26"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "regain-the-pawn,central-pawns"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "2...dxc4"]
[Start "orthodox 2.c4"]

2... dxc4 3. Nf3 { Develops and stops ...e5. Black's extra pawn on c4 is going nowhere, so White can calmly take it back. } 3... Nf6 ( 3... e6 4. e3 Nf6 5. Bxc4 ) 4. e3 { Opens the bishop on f1, which will take back the pawn on c4 at once. } 4... e6 5. Bxc4 { Pawn regained with a developing move. The bishop now watches the diagonal to e6 and f7. } 5... c5 ( 5... a6 6. O-O c5 7. Qe2 ) 6. O-O { Gets the king safe before the centre opens up. } 6... a6 7. Qe2 { Guards the bishop on c4 so ...b5 can be met, and clears d1 for the rook. } 7... b5 8. Bd3 { Moves the bishop away from the pawn push and aims it at the kingside. } 8... Nbd7 9. a4 { Hits the pawn on b5 and stops Black from calmly completing the development with ...Bb7 first. } 9... c4 10. Bc2 { Retreats out of the way and leaves the pawn on c4 where it blocks Black's own pieces. } 10... Bb7 11. e4 { Takes the centre. Plan: the e4 pawn gives White space, then play Nc3, Bg5 or Qe3 and push e5 when ready. Black's pawns on b5 and c4 are loose, so attack them. } *
